*** ch13-10-left-id — unification modulo left identity (Ul): variable position matters; syntactic + identity unifiers vs no unifier (Maude manual §13.4.5)

mod LEFTID-UNIFICATION-EX is
 sorts Magma Elem .
 subsorts Elem < Magma .
 op __ : Magma Magma -> Magma [gather (E e) left id: e] .
 ops a b c d e : -> Elem .
endm

unify in LEFTID-UNIFICATION-EX : X:Magma a =? Y:Magma a a .

*** manual writes "in LEFTID-UNIFICATION-EXAMPLE" here (typo); module is LEFTID-UNIFICATION-EX
irredundant unify in LEFTID-UNIFICATION-EX :
      X:Magma a =? Y:Magma a a .

unify in LEFTID-UNIFICATION-EX : a X:Magma =? a a Y:Magma .
